{
 "case": "SRC-03",
 "says": "A person selects docs/adr and README.md in the checkout of their work repository W (hosted as example/work). source.observe reads those files and returns an observation with local_effect none and provider_effect not_applicable: selecting the repository creates no Team, writes no metadata into the repository, makes no commit and uploads nothing. repository.bind then records the checkout as project evidence under W, again reaching no provider. Only afterwards does the person found a Team (team.found, whose target expects no Team to exist yet, so nothing earlier created one) and bind that Team's exchange carrier with carrier.bind: a carrier_binding naming the GitHub account, the provider's repository id, a namespace and the permitted effects, with carrier_state bound and nothing provisioned or uploaded. Even though the carrier names the same hosted repository, the work repository_binding and the Team's carrier_binding stay two records of two contracts, and neither changes the other.",
